            <div class="scroll-area">
                <div class="item-group" id="g1"><div class="hanging-bar"></div><span class="title">Stage-pass discipline shipped and visibly worked</span><span class="sub-text">Dx → Stage 1 (UNDERSTANDING-2 UX end-state) → Stage 2 (PLAN-1 broad strokes) → Stage 3 (PLAN-2 devil&#x27;s advocate twice) → Stage 4 (PLAN CHECK-5 overwrite check) → Stage 5 (execution). All five docs landed in cowork/10_April_1/ before a single line of code was written. The user&#x27;s explicit verdict: the planning depth &#x27;gave you real high value knowledge to work with&#x27;, and the conservative default on PLAN-2&#x27;s devil-advocate ideas &#x27;made good sense&#x27;.</span><div class="tag-row"><span class="tag">process</span><span class="tag">discipline</span></div><ul class="nested-list"><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind code">code</span><span class="code">/sessions/awesome-optimistic-rubin/mnt/Cufolio/cowork/10_April_1/PLAN CHECK-5.md</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">Verdict: GO. Proceed to Stage 5.</pre></details></li><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind chat">chat</span><span class="code">chat — user</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">planning-2 proposed some great ideas and the conservative erring against most of them made good sense.</pre></details></li></ul></div><div class="item-group" id="g2"><div class="hanging-bar"></div><span class="title">Stage-5 execution landed clean</span><span class="sub-text">Eleven files created or modified across electron IPC, React hooks, Canvases UI, ControlBar, LiveCanvas, App.jsx, and the AI tool layer. Full esbuild bundle of src/App.jsx came back at 480kb with zero errors after the final bfast-queue import fix. Every handler, component, and shortcut wired end-to-end in one pass.</span><div class="tag-row"><span class="tag">execution</span><span class="tag">build</span></div><ul class="nested-list"><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind shell">shell</span><span class="code">shell (live)</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">npx esbuild --bundle --packages=external --format=esm --loader:.jsx=jsx --loader:.css=empty src/App.jsx
../../../../../../tmp/briizos-bundle-check.js  480.1kb
⚡ Done in 45ms</pre></details></li></ul></div><div class="item-group" id="g3"><div class="hanging-bar"></div><span class="title">LiveCanvas reused via additive rawHtml/onSave props</span><span class="sub-text">Instead of building a second draggable-iframe overlay for the Floating form factor, extended the existing LiveCanvas singleton with an additive rawHtml prop (used directly as srcdoc when present) and an optional onSave prop that adds a header Save button. Non-breaking change for existing callers, zero new dependencies, and the Hybrid form factor falls out for free by dual-mounting with the Panel Tile path.</span><div class="tag-row"><span class="tag">architecture</span><span class="tag">reuse</span></div><ul class="nested-list"><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind code">code</span><span class="code">/sessions/awesome-optimistic-rubin/mnt/Cufolio/briizOS/briizOS.local/src/components/overlays/LiveCanvas.jsx</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">const srcdoc = canvasData?.rawHtml ?? buildTemplateHtml({ html, css, js });</pre></details></li></ul></div><div class="item-group" id="g4"><div class="hanging-bar"></div><span class="title">Canvas IPC extended via sidecar metadata, untouched sync contract</span><span class="sub-text">Added four new Electron handlers (canvas-delete, canvas-save-meta, canvas-load-meta, canvas-rename) alongside the existing canvas-save/list/load, storing form factor + source + timestamps in .meta.json sidecars next to each HTML file. The SyncContract §2 restriction limiting the panels collection to notes-only was sidestepped entirely — Canvases never touch the cloud panels collection.</span><div class="tag-row"><span class="tag">ipc</span><span class="tag">data</span></div><ul class="nested-list"><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind code">code</span><span class="code">/sessions/awesome-optimistic-rubin/mnt/Cufolio/briizOS/briizOS.local/electron/main.js</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">ipcMain.handle(&#x27;canvas-rename&#x27;, async (_, filename, newTitle) =&gt; { /* preserve prefix, slugify, move sidecar */ });</pre></details></li></ul></div><div class="item-group" id="g5"><div class="hanging-bar"></div><span class="title">Context-menu z-index bug fixed in two lines</span><span class="sub-text">User reported: hovering items in the ⋯ menu registered as hovering the card below. Diagnosed as a stacking-context leak — the menu was absolutely-positioned inside a card with no elevated z-index, so sibling cards drew on top and stole pointer events. Fix: add a menu-open class to the hosting card when the menu is open, and crown it z-index: 10 via one CSS rule. No portal, no JS, no drag-clamps.</span><div class="tag-row"><span class="tag">triage</span><span class="tag">css</span></div><ul class="nested-list"><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind code">code</span><span class="code">/sessions/awesome-optimistic-rubin/mnt/Cufolio/briizOS/briizOS.local/src/components/canvases/CanvasCard.jsx:88</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">className={menuOpen ? &#x27;canvas-card menu-open&#x27; : &#x27;canvas-card&#x27;}</pre></details></li><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind code">code</span><span class="code">/sessions/awesome-optimistic-rubin/mnt/Cufolio/briizOS/briizOS.local/src/components/canvases/CanvasesPopover.css:190</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">.canvas-card.menu-open { z-index: 10; }</pre></details></li></ul></div><div class="item-group" id="g6"><div class="hanging-bar"></div><span class="title">Scope-split for v0.2 made explicit instead of tacked on</span><span class="sub-text">When user added three new asks mid-triage (two-field AI create form with a new currentMain class reaching into settings, loading-state CSS + spinner with pending lifecycle, and an actual user-facing edit function), the response was to declare a new Stage 1 and decline to tack it onto this session. Stage-pass discipline survived its first pressure test.</span><div class="tag-row"><span class="tag">scope</span><span class="tag">discipline</span></div><ul class="nested-list"><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind chat">chat</span><span class="code">chat — user</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">but wer have already done a lot. do you want to push this part into a separate workspace</pre></details></li></ul></div>
