- [ ] Audit existing editor components in briizOS that could be reused
- [ ] Make &#x27;edit canvas as a human&#x27; the headline user story for Canvases v0.2, not an afterthought</span><div class="tag-row"><span class="tag">gap</span><span class="tag">feature</span></div><ul class="nested-list"><li class="nested-item"><details class="ref-details"><summary class="ref-summary"><span class="ref-kind chat">chat</span><span class="code">chat — user</span></summary><pre class="ref-snippet">a more significant issue right now is that from my eyevantage, there is no edit function attached to canvases: theyre made and inaccessible.</pre></details></li></ul></div><div class="item-group" id="b2"><div class="hanging-bar"></div><span class="title">Called the z-index bump &#x27;ugly&#x27; based on a visual norm that does not exist</span><span class="sub-text">When the floating LiveCanvas header appeared cut off, the proposed fix was a complicated top-offset + drag-clamp combo, because &#x27;option #1 (bump z-index) would leave the drag handle overlapping the ControlBar visually — ugly&#x27;. The user responded with a screenshot showing the existing Notes panel already overlapping the ControlBar as the established visual language. Overcorrected against a non-existent norm; the simple z-index fix was the right call all along.

