/**
 * briizOS Theme Engine
 *
 * Converts any CSS :root theme (any number of variables) into compact "DNA" —
 * each color decomposed to HSLA where L = "distance from black" (0 = black, 1 = white).
 *
 * DNA preserves a theme as equations:
 *   variable = template( colorSlot₀, colorSlot₁, … )
 *   colorSlot = { hue, saturation, lightness (dist-from-black), alpha }
 *
 * New themes are generated by remapping the equations to a fresh palette.
 *
 * Quick test:
 *   node --input-type=module -e "import('./src/lib/themeEngine.js').then(m => m.demo())"
 */

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
