    }

    .preview-frame-head {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 10px;
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
      color: var(--dna-muted, #9aa3bd);
      font-size: 12px;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    .frame-dots {
      display: flex;
      gap: 6px;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .frame-dot {
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: var(--dna-accent, #7aa2f7);
      opacity: 0.9;
    }

    .preview-embed {
      flex: 1;
      width: 100%;
      min-height: 282px;
      border: 0;
      background: transparent;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1260px) {
      #sidebar {
        width: 500px;
      }
      .preview-stage {
        width: min(920px, calc(100vw - 560px));
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 1120px) {
      .preview-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
      .preview-card,
      .preview-frame-wrap {
        min-height: auto;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="sidebar">
    <div class="box ghost">
      <h3>DNA Architect Pro+</h3>
      <p class="help">
        This version analyzes CSS variables once, infers their likely semantic roles,
        and then lets you retheme <strong>text / panels / buttons / inputs / frames</strong>
        independently, live. Auto-detection is heuristic — you can override any mapping manually.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
      <h4>1. Source DNA Dictionary</h4>
      <textarea id="rawInput">:root {
  --bg: #0f1118;
  --surface: #171a24;
  --panel-bg: #1b1f2b;
  --text: #dbe3ff;
  --text-muted: #8590b2;
  --accent: #7aa2f7;
  --primary: #7aa2f7;
  --btn-bg: var(--primary);
  --btn-text: #081018;
  --border: #374159;
  --input-bg: #121621;
  --input-border: #424b67;
  --iframe-bg: #0d1017;
  --iframe-border: #323a53;
}</textarea>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
      <h4>2. Smart Semantic Mapping <small id="varSummary"></small></h4>
      <p class="micro-note">
        Auto mode favors repeated values, short foundational names, and “primary/accent/main/default”
        style labels. Any slot can be manually redirected.
      </p>
      <div id="mappingGrid" class="mapping-grid"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="box">
      <h4>3. Typography</h4>
      <div class="control compact" style="margin-bottom: 12px;">
        <input
          type="text"
          id="fontInput"
          list="fontSuggestions"
          value="system-ui"
          placeholder="Type any CSS font-family"
        />
        <label class="toggle-inline">
          <input type="checkbox" id="fontAutoLoad" checked />
          auto-load web font
        </label>
      </div>

      <datalist id="fontSuggestions">
        <option value="system-ui"></option>
        <option value="'Inter', sans-serif"></option>
        <option value="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif"></option>
        <option value="'Playfair Display', serif"></option>
        <option value="'IBM Plex Sans', sans-serif"></option>
        <option value="'Fira Code', monospace"></option>
        <option value="'JetBrains Mono', monospace"></option>
      </datalist>

      <div class="control-group">
        <div class="control">
          <label>Hue</label>
          <input type="range" data-group="text" data-prop="h" data-unit="°" min="-180" max="180" value="0" />
          <span class="val">0°</span>
        </div>
        <div class="control">
          <label>Sat</label>
          <input type="range" data-group="text" data-prop="s" data-unit="%" min="-100" max="100" value="0" />
